arm64: dts: h713: describe the DE picture-scaler window as an optional cross-check

A read-only syscon over the display engine's picture scaler at 0x05180000
and the optional allwinner,scaler phandle on the HDMI receiver node. The
receiver driver (0136f) reads one word of it, +0x34, the scaler's input
window, and only as a CROSS-CHECK: after INCAP's rowbyte has said that the
firmware scales the source down inside its capture path (HY300 Pro, 1920x1080
source on a 1280x720 panel, 864-byte lines) the window names the ring's exact
size, 852x478, where the rowbyte can name it only to within 16 pixels - and
only when it agrees with the rowbyte and the source's shape. Where the rowbyte
says the ring is the source (the HY310, every case) it is never read.

The register is not the ring's primary source because the firmware rewrites
it only when it rebuilds its window chain; measured stale on the HY310 (dev17,
20.09.2026). The driver works without this node - then the ring's width is
the pitch (864 instead of 852, twelve padding bytes shown as picture) - so the
node is optional and can be dropped with this one patch; it lives in
sun50i-h713.dtsi so both boards get it. One software for both boards.

Follow-up to 0136b (same node), needs nothing else; 0136f reads it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1743,6 +1743,29 @@
 		};
 
 		/*
+		 * The display engine's picture scaler, the block at
+		 * 0x05180000. Like INCAP above it belongs to the MIPS firmware
+		 * and has no ARM driver; the HDMI receiver node reads one word
+		 * of it, +0x34 (the scaler's input window), and writes none.
+		 * The receiver driver uses it as a CROSS-CHECK only: after
+		 * INCAP's rowbyte has said that the firmware scales the source
+		 * down inside its capture path (HY300 Pro, 1920x1080 source on a
+		 * 1280x720 panel: 864-byte lines), this word names the ring's
+		 * exact size (852x478) where the rowbyte can name it only to
+		 * within 16 pixels. The firmware rewrites it only when it
+		 * rebuilds its window chain, so it can be stale (HY310, dev17,
+		 * 20.09.2026: 1280x720 left standing after 720p -> 1080p); the
+		 * driver takes it only when it agrees with the rowbyte and the
+		 * source's shape, and never on a board where the rowbyte says
+		 * the ring is the source. Optional in the driver.
+		 */
+		de_scaler: syscon@5180000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-de-scaler",
+				     "syscon";
+			reg = <0x05180000 0x1000>;
+		};
+
+		/*
 		 * LINK, the HDMI receiver's port window. Like INCAP above it
 		 * belongs to the MIPS firmware and has no ARM driver: the
 		 * firmware detects the audio in the stream, programmes the
@@ -2135,6 +2158,13 @@
 	 *                    read only, byte wide: without it everything
 	 *                    works except the three audio status controls,
 	 *                    which stay at zero.
+	 *   allwinner,scaler  the syscon over the DE picture scaler (syscon@
+	 *                    5180000 above). Optional, read only: a cross-check
+	 *                    for the ring's size where INCAP's rowbyte says the
+	 *                    firmware scales the source down in its capture
+	 *                    path. Without it that size is arithmetic from the
+	 *                    rowbyte (the width to within 16 pixels); where the
+	 *                    firmware does not scale it is never read.
 	 *
 	 * No interrupt: three independent searches of the firmware image found
 	 * the capture interrupt only inside the MIPS interrupt controller, and
@@ -2147,6 +2177,7 @@
 		memory-region-names = "hdmi-ring", "cpu-comm-shmem";
 		allwinner,incap = <&incap>;
 		allwinner,hdmirx-link = <&hdmirx_link>;
+		allwinner,scaler = <&de_scaler>;
 		status = "okay";
 	};
 
